Core 1.4.1 libnfs rejects fragmented RPC record markers. UNFS3/libtirpc
fragments large replies at 64 KiB. Conservative 32 KiB transfers avoid
this failure without changing the RPC ABI or adding runtime privileges.
This is a bounded compatibility workaround, not general fragment support.

Source equivalent for sahlberg/libnfs libnfs-6.0.2, lib/libnfs.c.
The release-image integrator changes the corresponding pinned arm64 MOV
immediate after checking the entire original library SHA256.

--- a/lib/libnfs.c
+++ b/lib/libnfs.c
@@ -623,8 +623,8 @@
 
 	nfs->nfsi->default_version = NFS_V3;
 	nfs->nfsi->version = NFS_V3;
-	nfs->nfsi->readmax = NFS_DEF_XFER_SIZE;
-	nfs->nfsi->writemax = NFS_DEF_XFER_SIZE;
+	nfs->nfsi->readmax = 32 * 1024;
+	nfs->nfsi->writemax = 32 * 1024;
 	nfs->nfsi->readdir_dircount = 8192;
 	nfs->nfsi->readdir_maxcount = 8192;
 
